            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e5639d5b",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "a = 3.5\r\nshow(a)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c6449f06",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `summary` function returns the type of a variable. For arrays, their size is also returned.\n\nExample. Let’s display information about the matrix `x`:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "64725a54",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "x = [1 2 3; 4 5 6]\r\nsummary(x)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a31e190a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Formatted output\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "31afe9e6",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "You can control the precision of variable display using the `@printf` function. This function will be available if you include the `Printf` package.\n\nExample. Let’s display the value of the variable `x = 12.67835675` to $4$ decimal places:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2eb9c8d6",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "using Printf\r\nx = 12.67835675\r\n@printf(\"%.4f\", x)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4ea16d48",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The expression in quotation marks `\"%.4f\"` specifies the format for outputting the variable: `.4` denotes the number of decimal places, whilst the letter `f` specifies the data type of the variable `x`. In this case, `f` denotes the real data type; other options include `i` (integer data type), `e` (exponential notation), `s` (string data type), and so on. The second argument of the `@printf` function is the name of the variable `x`, the value of which is to be displayed on screen. You can find full information on the output format using the `@printf` function in the [documentation](https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/io/fprintf).\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7680b842",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ✏️Task 2\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
