          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b394a268",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Reading and writing files\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7e88a975",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Working with text files\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4b6b8e06",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The **Julia** language provides facilities for reading data from a file and writing to a file. \n\n#### Opening a file for reading\n\nTo start working with a file, you must first open it. To do this, use the function `open(filename)`, where `filename` is the name of the physical file in the local **AnyMath** environment, enclosed in double quotation marks. The result of the `open` function is assigned to a variable of type `IOStream` (input/output stream).\n\nExample. From the folder for this course, let’s open the text file `data.txt`:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "da0504d5",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "f = open(\"data.txt\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "006c3047",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "To read all lines from the **text** file, use the `readlines` function; to read a single line, use the `readline` function. The argument for these functions is a variable of type `IOStream`.\n\nExample. Let’s read all the lines from the file `data.txt` and assign them to the variable `x`:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f64ff0a6",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "x = readlines(f)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0f573320",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This file contains three lines. They are read into the vector `x`, which consists of elements of string type. Each element of the vector represents a separate line of the text.\n\nExample. Let’s read a single line from the file `data.txt`:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c48bd748",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "f = open(\"data.txt\")\r\nx = readline(f)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7447f245",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{% note info \"Note\" %}\n\nIn the examples above, the `open` function opened a file located in the current folder (the same folder as this interactive script). If you wish to open a file located in a different folder, you must specify the full path to the file, including its name, as an argument to the function. \n\n{% endnote %}\n\nFor example, you can access the same `data.txt` file using the full path:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ebde61e1",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "f = open(\"/user/start/Courses/Basics of programming in AnyMath/data.txt\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "56003018",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Please note that in the **AnyMath** local environment, the root folder is called `/user`, and the training courses are located in the folders `/user/start/Courses/Course Name`.\n\n**Julia** allows you to change the current directory using the `cd` command. For example:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "15c9d8d2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "cd(\"/user/start/Courses/Basics of programming in AnyMath\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4d3810fa",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "After this, you can access files from this directory by name only, without specifying the path:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "228f8c1f",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "f = open(\"data.txt\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
