        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2522187",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "####\n\nYou can read more about input/output functions and working with files in the [documentation](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/en/julia/base/io-network.html).\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f83594f9",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Working with numerical files\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cc4841d6",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For working with numerical data organized in tabular form, `csv` files are widely used. To access functions that allow you to work with tabular data, you need to load the `CSV` and `DataFrames` packages. The `CSV.read(filename, DataFrame)` allows you to read data from a file into a `DataFrame`-type variable.\n\nExample. Let’s read data from the file `data_table.csv`:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fa968a4f",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "using CSV, DataFrames\r\ndata = CSV.read(\"data_table.csv\", DataFrame)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "02384b87",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We can see that each column of the table has its own name: `Jan`, `Feb`, `Mar` and `Apr`. A column from a `DataFrame` was extracted using dot notation: `table.Variable_Name`. For example:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "74da94d2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "x = data.Jan"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ace7ffd0",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "y = data.Feb"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1222a446",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If you need to retrieve not the entire column but only some of its elements, you can use the following syntax:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fa71a3db",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "z = data[1, \"Mar\"]"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "02abf128",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Here, the variable `z` is assigned the value of the first element in the `Mar` column of the `data` table.\n\nIf you need to retrieve several consecutive elements in a column, the first index is written as a range: `start:end`. For example, let’s assign the elements from the $2$nd to the $4$th in the `Apr` column of the `data` table to the variable `t`:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "316c28a7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "t = data[2:4, \"Apr\"]"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "db131ca3",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### ✏️Task 7\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "20ee1812",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Assign the third element of the `Jan` column in the `data` table to the variable `v`, and the elements from the second to the fifth in the `Feb` column of the same table to the variable `w`.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
